# ${SRC_DIR}/models/

Data models for ${PROJECT_NAME}.

## What lives here

- One file per collection / table, named `<entity>.model.ts`.
- Mongoose schemas, pg row interfaces, or both — the file owns the entity.

## What does NOT live here

- Business logic — that belongs in a feature's `services/`.
- HTTP shapes (request/response types) — those live in the feature's `types/`.

## Naming

- `<entity>.model.ts` — singular, lowercase. Examples: `user.model.ts`, `order.model.ts`.

## File size

If a single model file grows past 500 lines, split it into per-concern files
(`user.schema.ts`, `user.indexes.ts`, `user.statics.ts`) and re-export from a
barrel.

